{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed the Intervals.icu integration:\n\n- Connect now uses authenticated `POST` initialization and frontend redirect (`static/app.js:34`, `server.py:150`).\n- Removed duplicate read/write scopes (`config.py:11`).\n- Corrected the token exchange to send only the three supported fields (`server.py:57`).\n- Removed the artificial one-hour expiry and refresh job; tokens now remain valid until revoked.\n- Added provider-401 handling that clears the token and prompts reconnection (`server.py:190`).\n\n`ANSWER.md` documents the causes, fixes, verification, and which colleague-note recommendations applied.\n\nVerification passed with a local mock provider covering the complete OAuth flow, wellness access, and revocation handling. Python/JavaScript syntax checks and `git diff --check` also passed. A live Intervals.icu account was not tested because the repository contains placeholder credentials."}
